From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:33:46 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] kcm: Show what each screen shows in the arrangement view

The arrangement view draws each screen as an empty rectangle with its
name, so telling two screens of the same model apart, or finding the one
a window is on, takes Identify Screens and a look around the room.

With Show Screen Contents, in the view's menu, each rectangle shows a
picture of its screen, taken through KWin's ScreenShot2 interface once a
second while the view is on screen, at no more than 512 pixels on its
longer side. The picture is read on a worker thread, so the view never
waits for it. Before Plasma 6.8, KWin gives the interface only to
programs that list it under X-KDE-DBUS-Restricted-Interfaces in their
desktop file entry (KWin's 0ea31ae7 drops that check); when KWin refuses,
the view says why and works as before.

Until the person chooses, the pictures are shown on mains power and not
on battery, following UPower's OnBattery; their choice is kept in
kcm_kscreenrc. A screen in a 3D mode, which Stereo KWin captures as both
eyes side by side, shows its left eye.

wdisplays, the wlroots display tool, has the same option.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
